initial-order-7be5ccf1.conceptual_definition:
The formula 
$$S(t_{BB}) ≈ S_{min}
$$ indicates that at the time of the Big Bang, denoted by $t_{BB}$, the entropy of the universe, $S(t_{BB})$, is approximately equal to its minimum possible value, $S_{min}$. This suggests that the early universe was in a state of very low entropy, which is a prerequisite for the subsequent evolution and development of complex structures according to the second law of thermodynamics.

